On Ubuntu 20.04

1. Build bouncycastle and install jars

1.1 git clone https://github.com/bcgit/bc-java.git

1.2 cd bc-java

1.3 git checkout -b 1.79 r1rv79

1.4 export JDKPATH=/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64
    export JAVA_VERSION_PREFIX=11

1.5 install ant and maven

1.6 sh ./build1-8+

the jar files are generated in build/artifacts/jdk1.8/jars/

1.7 push jars file to .m2

1.7.1 cd build/artifacts/jdk1.8/jars

1.7.2 run following commands

mvn install:install-file -Dfile=bcpkix-jdk18on-1.79.jar -DgroupId=org.bouncycastle -DartifactId=bcpkix-jdk18on -Dversion=1.79 -Dpackaging=jar
mvn install:install-file -Dfile=bctls-jdk18on-1.79.jar -DgroupId=org.bouncycastle -DartifactId=bctls-jdk18on -Dversion=1.79 -Dpackaging=jar
mvn install:install-file -Dfile=bcprov-jdk18on-1.79.jar -DgroupId=org.bouncycastle -DartifactId=bcprov-jdk18on -Dversion=1.79 -Dpackaging=jar
mvn install:install-file -Dfile=bcutil-jdk18on-1.79.jar -DgroupId=org.bouncycastle -DartifactId=bcutil-jdk18on -Dversion=1.79 -Dpackaging=jar
mvn install:install-file -Dfile=bcprov-ext-jdk18on-1.79.jar -DgroupId=org.bouncycastle -DartifactId=bcprov-ext-jdk18on -Dversion=1.79 -Dpackaging=jar

2. checkout oqs-bouncycastle

2.1 git clone https://github.com/Open-QKD-Network/oqs-bouncycastle.git

2.2 git checkout 2025
2.3 cd java-crypto-tools-src/gen
2.4 copy jars generated in 1.6 to lib directory
2.5 mvn clean package

3. Build liboqs

3.1 git clone https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs.git

3.2 copy example_kem.c from oqs-bouncycastle/ to tests/example_kem.c

3.3 in example_kem.c you need to change small code to run tests

3.4 ninja build

4. Run build/tests/example_kem for different use cases

5. cd java-crypto-tools-src/gen

5.1 ./run.sh

6. We have two tests by making small change to run.sh

6.1) liboqs generates public key, and bouncycastle reads public key and generates shared secret

6.2) bouncycastle generates public key, and liboqs reads public key and generates shared secret
